<Layout title="Accessibility"><PageIntro eyebrow="A more welcoming web" title="Room for everyone to take part." description="This website is designed to make its content and core journeys usable across devices and different ways of navigating." /><section class="section container prose"><h2>Features built into the site.</h2><ul><li>Semantic headings, labeled navigation, and a skip-to-content link.</li><li>Visible keyboard focus and keyboard-operable menus, forms, and filters.</li><li>Text alternatives for meaningful photographs.</li><li>Responsive layouts and support for reduced-motion preferences.</li><li>A readable project directory that does not depend on an interactive map.</li><li>Clearly labeled forms, native validation, and explicit email-draft status.</li></ul><h2>External services.</h2><p>Payment providers, newsletter platforms, archive pages, and social networks have their own interfaces. We cannot guarantee their accessibility. Contact the foundation if you need another way to receive information or participate.</p><h2>Tell us what would help.</h2><p>If something is difficult to read or use, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> with the page address, the issue, and your preferred way to receive the information. No claim of formal accessibility certification is made.</p></section></Layout>
